	[
		'slug'        => 'holiday-let-linen-laundry',
		'title'       => 'Holiday Let Linen and Laundry: Managing Quick Turnarounds',
		'seo_title'   => 'Holiday Let Linen and Laundry: Quick Turnaround Tips',
		'description' => 'Holiday let linen and laundry made manageable: how many sets you need, washing and drying on tight turnarounds, stain fixes and hire versus owning your own.',
		'category'    => 'holiday-lets',
		'service'     => 'holiday-let-airbnb-cleaning',
		'related'     => [ 'holiday-let-changeover-checklist', 'airbnb-5-star-cleanliness', 'static-caravan-cleaning-guide' ],
		'image'       => 'folded white towels',
		'excerpt'     => 'How many linen sets a holiday let needs, how to wash and dry them on tight turnarounds, and whether linen hire or owning your own works better.',
		'content'     => <<<'HTML'
<p>Holiday let linen becomes manageable with a simple rule of thumb: keep three sets per bed, one on the bed, one in the wash and one clean on the shelf, plus plenty of spare towels. Add a fixed washing routine and a reliable way of drying, and same-day changeovers stop being a scramble.</p>
<p>Laundry is where changeovers tend to fall behind. A wash that won't dry on a damp day in <a href="{{area:bridlington}}">Bridlington</a>, or a cottage near <a href="{{area:driffield}}">Driffield</a> with back-to-back weekend bookings, can delay check-in more easily than any cleaning task. This guide covers how much linen you need, how to wash and dry it, and whether to hire or buy.</p>
<div class="cc-takeaways"><p class="cc-takeaways__title">Key takeaways</p><ul><li>Keep at least three sets of bed linen per bed, and more towels than you think you need.</li><li>Choose white, hard-wearing cotton or poly-cotton that can be washed hot and stays bright.</li><li>Wash bedding and towels at 60°C where the label allows, and never store linen that is even slightly damp.</li><li>Linen hire saves time; owning your own gives you control. Choose based on your bookings and storage.</li></ul></div>
<h2>How many sets of linen does a holiday let need?</h2>
<p>Three sets per bed is the minimum that works for regular changeovers: one in use, one being laundered and one ready to go. With back-to-back bookings in summer, or if laundry is done off site and takes a day or two to come back, a fourth set gives you breathing space.</p>
<p>For each bed, plan for:</p>
<ul>
<li>Fitted sheets, duvet covers and pillowcases, with extra pillowcases as they mark more easily.</li>
<li>Two mattress protectors and enough pillow protectors to swap them when needed.</li>
<li>A spare duvet and pillows, so one set can be cleaned without leaving the bed short.</li>
</ul>
<p>For each guest, allow a bath towel and a hand towel per stay, plus a beach towel if you offer them, and multiply by three. Add bath mats, tea towels and cleaning cloths to the count. If someone else handles your changeovers, such as a <a href="{{service:holiday-let-airbnb-cleaning}}">holiday let cleaning service</a>, agree where spare stock is kept and who tops it up.</p>
<h2>Choosing holiday let linen that survives frequent washing</h2>
<p>Holiday let linen is washed far more often than bedding at home, so durability matters most.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Go white.</strong> White linen can be washed hot, looks fresh in photos and makes marks easy to spot before it goes on a bed.</li>
<li><strong>Pick a hard-wearing fabric.</strong> Percale cotton feels crisp, while poly-cotton blends dry faster and crease less, which helps on tight turnarounds.</li>
<li><strong>Standardise sizes.</strong> Buying the same range for every bed makes sorting and counting much faster.</li>
<li><strong>Mark bed sizes.</strong> A coloured stitch or laundry marker on the label, such as blue for king and red for double, saves unfolding sheets to check.</li>
<li><strong>Choose quick-drying towels.</strong> Very thick towels feel luxurious but can take much longer to dry.</li>
</ul>
<p>Grey or bobbled linen quickly drags down reviews, as we explain in our guide to <a href="{{guide:airbnb-5-star-cleanliness}}">getting five-star cleanliness reviews</a>. Replace it as soon as it looks tired.</p>
<h2>Washing holiday let linen: temperatures and routine</h2>
<p>Bed linen and towels should be washed at 60°C between guests where the care label allows. A hot wash with a good detergent gives a hygienic reset for the next guest and keeps white linen looking bright.</p>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Suggested wash</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Sheets, duvet covers, pillowcases</td><td>60°C every stay</td><td>Check for stains before washing, as heat can set some marks</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bath towels, hand towels, bath mats</td><td>60°C every stay</td><td>Go easy on fabric conditioner, which can reduce absorbency over time</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tea towels and cloths</td><td>60°C every stay</td><td>Wash separately from bed linen</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mattress and pillow protectors</td><td>Per care label, whenever marked and on a regular schedule</td><td>Some waterproof protectors need a lower temperature</td></tr>
<tr><td>Duvets and pillows</td><td>Per care label, periodically</td><td>Large items may need a bigger machine or a launderette</td></tr>
<tr><td>Throws and cushion covers</td><td>Per care label, regularly</td><td>Easy to forget, but guests notice marks</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Don't overload the machine, as linen needs room to move to come out clean. Measure detergent rather than guessing, because too much leaves a residue that can irritate skin. If you prefer gentler products, our guide to <a href="{{guide:gentle-cleaning-hard-water-homes}}">eco-friendly cleaning</a> explains what actually works. Regular hot washing also helps guests with allergies, which we cover in <a href="{{guide:bedroom-dust-mite-reduction}}">cleaning for dust mites and allergies</a>.</p>
<h2>Drying and ironing on tight turnarounds</h2>
<p>Drying is usually the bottleneck. A washing line can't be relied on at the coast or in winter, and linen that comes in slightly damp will smell musty by the next changeover.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Use a tumble dryer.</strong> For a busy let, a reliable tumble dryer is close to essential. Clean the lint filter after every load.</li>
<li><strong>Dry completely.</strong> Never fold or store linen that feels cool or damp, as it can develop mildew in the cupboard.</li>
<li><strong>Fold straight from the dryer.</strong> Taking linen out promptly and folding it while warm cuts creases and ironing time.</li>
<li><strong>Iron what shows.</strong> Pillowcases and the top edge of duvet covers make the most difference in photos and on arrival.</li>
<li><strong>Store it well.</strong> Keep clean linen in a dry, ventilated, lockable cupboard, not in a damp outbuilding.</li>
</ul>
<p>Damp storage is a particular problem by the sea, and our guide to <a href="{{guide:seaside-property-cleaning}}">cleaning a seaside property</a> has advice on keeping coastal lets dry.</p>
<div class="cc-callout"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Store each bed's complete set inside one of its own pillowcases. Whoever does the changeover grabs one bundle per bed and knows everything matches.</p></div>
<h2>Dealing with stains and damaged linen</h2>
<p>Stains are inevitable. The key is to treat them before the first hot wash, as heat can set blood and some make-up for good.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Blood:</strong> rinse in cold water as soon as possible, then wash as normal.</li>
<li><strong>Make-up and fake tan:</strong> pre-treat with washing-up liquid or a stain remover, working it in gently before washing.</li>
<li><strong>Red wine, tea and coffee:</strong> blot, rinse with cold water and pre-treat.</li>
<li><strong>Rust or grey marks:</strong> often caused by damp storage or an old machine. Retire badly marked items rather than putting them back on a bed.</li>
</ul>
<p>Keep a separate bag for anything stained, torn or thinning, so you can see when stock needs topping up.</p>
<h2>Linen hire or owning your own: which is better?</h2>
<h3>Linen hire</h3>
<ul>
<li>Clean, pressed sets are delivered and dirty sets collected, saving hours of washing.</li>
<li>There is no need for a washing machine, tumble dryer or large storage space at the property.</li>
<li>You have less control over quality and depend on delivery days fitting your bookings.</li>
<li>Some providers have minimum orders or contracts, so compare terms carefully.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Owning your own linen</h3>
<ul>
<li>You have full control over quality, colour and how it looks in your photos.</li>
<li>It is flexible around last-minute bookings, with no delivery schedule to work to.</li>
<li>It needs time, a good washer and dryer, and storage space.</li>
<li>You pay for replacements as items wear out.</li>
</ul>
<p>One property with steady bookings often suits owning your linen; several lets, or properties without laundry facilities, may suit hire.</p>
<h2>Fitting laundry into your changeover routine</h2>
<ol>
<li>Strip all the beds and gather the towels as the first job of the changeover.</li>
<li>Start the first wash immediately, or bag linen for the hire collection.</li>
<li>Remake the beds from your clean stock, not the laundry you have just started.</li>
<li>Move washing to the dryer as each load finishes while you carry on cleaning.</li>
<li>Fold and store dry linen before you leave, and note any items running low.</li>
</ol>
<p>Our <a href="{{guide:holiday-let-changeover-checklist}}">holiday let changeover checklist</a> shows where laundry fits alongside the rest of the clean. For caravans without a washing machine, or ones closed over winter, see the <a href="{{guide:static-caravan-cleaning-guide}}">static caravan cleaning guide</a>; taking linen home at the end of the season stops it getting damp.</p>
<h2>Help with holiday let changeovers in East Yorkshire</h2>
<p>Linen is just one part of a smooth turnaround. Our <a href="{{service:holiday-let-airbnb-cleaning}}">holiday let and Airbnb cleaners</a> make up beds to your standard, check stock and report anything that needs replacing, and they work around your laundry arrangements whether you use a hire service or keep linen on site. We cover coastal lets, town flats and countryside cottages from Bridlington to <a href="{{area:pocklington}}">Pocklington</a>, and can add a periodic <a href="{{service:deep-cleaning}}">deep clean</a> between seasons.</p>
<p>Every job comes with a fixed quote agreed in advance. <a href="{{page:contact}}">Contact us</a> to talk through your property and booking pattern.</p>
