			[ 'How do you clean salt off windows?', 'Rinse the glass with plenty of clean water first to dissolve the salt, then wash with warm water and a little washing-up liquid, squeegee and buff dry. Wiping salt off when dry can scratch the glass.' ],
			[ 'How do I stop damp in a seaside holiday let?', 'Keep air moving with vents and extractor fans, keep a low background heat in cold months and use a dehumidifier when the property is empty. Wipe condensation at every changeover and leave gaps between furniture and outside walls.' ],
			[ 'Does sea air damage furniture and fittings?', 'Salt in sea air attracts moisture and speeds up corrosion, so metal fittings and outdoor furniture wear faster than they would inland. Regular wiping and drying slows the damage considerably.' ],
			[ 'How often should windows be cleaned in a coastal property?', 'More often than inland, because salt film builds up quickly. Monthly is a sensible starting point, with an extra clean after storms or whenever the glass starts to look hazy.' ],
